{"stigs":[{"release_info":"Release: 15 Benchmark Date: 01 Apr 2026","uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"UNCLASSIFIED","stig_name":"Microsoft IIS 10.0 Site Security Technical Implementation Guide","version":"2","rules":[{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website session state cookie settings must be configured to Use Cookies mode.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218736r1022669","group_title":"SRG-APP-000001-WSR-000002","uuid":"916BA9A7-6BF8-1014-8A80-BDF47BF814FA","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"When the session information is stored on the client, the session ID, along with the user authorization and identity information, is sent along with each client request and is stored in either a cookie, embedded in the uniform resource locator (URL), or placed in a hidden field on the displayed form. Each of these offers advantages and disadvantages. The biggest disadvantage to all three is the hijacking of a session along with all of the user's credentials.\n\nWhen the user authorization and identity information is stored on the server in a protected and encrypted database, the communication between the client and website will only send the session identifier, and the server can then retrieve user credentials for the session when needed. If, during transmission, the session were to be hijacked, the user's credentials would not be compromised.\n\nASP.NET provides a session state, which is available as the HttpSessionState class, as a method of storing session-specific information visible only within the session. ASP.NET session state identifies requests from the same browser during a limited time window as a session and provides the ability to persist variable values for the duration of that session.\n\nWhen using the URI mode for cookie settings under session state, IIS will reject and reissue session IDs that do not have active sessions. Configuring IIS to expire session IDs and regenerate tokens gives a potential attacker less time to capture a cookie and gain access to server content.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218736"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-218736r1022669_rule","ccis":["CCI-000054"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nClick the site name.\nUnder the \"ASP.NET\" section, select \"Session State\".\nUnder \"Cookie Settings\", verify the \"Use Cookies\" mode is selected from the \"Mode:\" drop-down list.\nIf the \"Use Cookies\" mode is selected, this is not a finding.\n\nAlternative method:\nClick the site name.\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.web/sessionState\".\nVerify the \"cookieless\" is set to \"UseCookies\".\nIf the \"cookieless\" is not set to \"UseCookies\", this is a finding.\nNote: If IIS 10.0 server/site is used only for system-to-system maintenance, does not allow users to connect to interface, and is restricted to specific system IPs, this is Not Applicable.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server: \n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nUnder the ASP.NET section, select \"Session State\".\n\nUnder \"Cookie Settings\", select the \"Use Cookies\" from the \"Mode:\" drop-down list.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218736","group_id_src":"V-218736","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000202","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000001-WSR-000002","id":"V-218736"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109297","V-100193"],"comments":null},{"reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000203","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109299","V-100195"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000014-WSR-000006","id":"V-218737"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218737","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218737","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is a public IIS 10.0 web server, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If SSL is installed on load balancer/proxy server through which traffic is routed to the IIS 10.0 server, and the IIS 10.0 server receives traffic from the load balancer/proxy server, the SSL requirement must be met on the load balancer/proxy server and is Not Applicable in this STIG.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nClick the site name.\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon.\nVerify \"Require SSL\" check box is selected.\n\nIf the \"Require SSL\" check box is not selected, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon.\n\nSelect \"Require SSL\" check box.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","uuid":"916BB4B6-6BF8-1014-A016-DBD210142683","group_title":"SRG-APP-000014-WSR-000006","rule_title":"A private IIS 10.0 website must only accept Secure Socket Layer (SSL) connections.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218737r1022671","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218737","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218737r1022671_rule","ccis":["CCI-000068"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   false (SSL is enabled - Click the site name. Double-click the 'SSL Settings' icon. Verify 'Require SSL is selected' If the 'Require SSL ' is not selected, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21873701 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL is enabled - Click the site name. Double-click the 'SSL Settings' icon. Verify 'Require SSL is selected' If the 'Require SSL ' is not selected, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21873701 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'access'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'sslflags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21873701 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must contain text ssl\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Ssl'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Transport Layer Security (TLS) encryption is a required security setting for a private web server. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. A private web server must use a FIPS 140-2-approved TLS version, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.\n\nNIST SP 800-52 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems."},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Note: If the server being reviewed is a private IIS 10.0 web server, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon.\n\nSelect \"Require SSL\" check box.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is a private IIS 10.0 web server, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is a public IIS 10.0 web server not requiring authentication, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting WSUS, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting Simple Certificate Enrollment Services (SCEP), this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting Network Device Enrollment Services (NDES), this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon.\n\nVerify \"Require SSL\" check box is selected.\n\nIf the \"Require SSL\" check box is not selected, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218738"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218738r1022673_rule","ccis":["CCI-000068"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (SSL is enabled - Click the site name. Double-click the 'SSL Settings' icon. Verify 'Require SSL is selected' If the 'Require SSL ' is not selected, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21873801 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL is enabled - Click the site name. Double-click the 'SSL Settings' icon. Verify 'Require SSL is selected' If the 'Require SSL ' is not selected, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21873801 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'access'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'sslflags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21873801 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must contain text ssl\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Ssl'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n","discussion":"Transport Layer Security (TLS) encryption is a required security setting for a private web server. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. A private web server must use a FIPS 140-2-approved TLS version, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.\n\nNIST SP 800-52 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000014-WSR-000006","uuid":"916BBCE2-6BF8-1014-8420-D7CE4170A28E","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"A public IIS 10.0 website must only accept Secure Socket Layer (SSL) connections when authentication is required.","rule_id":"SV-218738r1022673","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000014-WSR-000006","id":"V-218738"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109301","V-100197"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000204","group_id_src":"V-218738","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218738"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Note: \"Microsoft-IIS-Logging/logs\" must be enabled prior to configuring this setting.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nUnder Log Event Destination, select the \"Both log file and ETW event\" radio button.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nUnder Log Event Destination, verify the \"Both log file and ETW event\" radio button is selected.\n\nIf the \"Both log file and ETW event\" radio button is not selected, this is a finding.\n\nNote: \"Microsoft-IIS-Logging/logs\" must be enabled prior to configuring this setting. More configuration information is available at:\nhttps://blogs.intelink.gov/blogs/_disairrt/?p=1317","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for each IIS 10.0 website must be enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/logfile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/logfile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/logfile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21873901 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for each IIS 10.0 website must be enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21873901 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website logfile.logTargetW3C.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'logfile.logTargetW3C'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21873901 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result equal File, ETW.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'File, ETW'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logTargetW3C'\n                        : result equals 'File'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logTargetW3C'\n                        : result equals 'File'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logTargetW3C'\n                        : result equals 'File'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/logfile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/logfile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/logfile.logTargetW3C = 'File' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'File, ETW' \n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Internet Information Services (IIS) on Windows Server 2012 provides basic logging capabilities. However, because IIS takes some time to flush logs to disk, administrators do not have access to logging information in real-time. In addition, text-based log files can be difficult and time-consuming to process.\n\nIn IIS 10.0, the administrator has the option of sending logging information to Event Tracing for Windows (ETW). This option gives the administrator the ability to use standard query tools, or create custom tools, for viewing real-time logging information in ETW. This provides a significant advantage over parsing text-based log files that are not updated in real time.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055, SRG-APP-000108-WSR-000166","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218739"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218739r1022675_rule","ccis":["CCI-000139","CCI-001464"],"rule_title":"Both the log file and Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) for each IIS 10.0 website must be enabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218739r1022675","uuid":"916BC571-6BF8-1014-8351-CAED59C855A2","group_title":"SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109303","V-100199"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055","id":"V-218739"},"rule_version":"IIST-SI-000206","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218739","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218739","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06"},{"mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218740","title":"SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000060"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109305","V-100201"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000208","group_id_src":"V-218740","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218740","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Access the proxy server through which inbound web traffic is passed and configure settings to pass web traffic to the IIS 10.0 web server transparently.","check_content":"Interview the System Administrator to review the configuration of the IIS 10.0 architecture and determine if inbound web traffic is passed through a proxy.\n\nIf the IIS 10.0 is receiving inbound web traffic through a proxy, the audit logs must be reviewed to determine if correct source information is being passed through by the proxy server.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nClick \"View log file\".\n\nWhen log file is displayed, review source IP information in log entries and verify entries do not reflect the IP address of the proxy server.\n\nIf the website is not behind a load balancer or proxy server, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf the log entries in the log file(s) reflect the IP address of the proxy server as the source, this is a finding.\n\nIf provisions have been made to log the client IP via another field (i.e., utilizing X-Forwarded-For), this is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:901","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218740r960900_rule","ccis":["CCI-000133"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218740, SV-218740r960900, SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000060)\n","discussion":"Web server logging capability is critical for accurate forensic analysis. Without sufficient and accurate information, a correct replay of the events cannot be determined. \n\nAscertaining the correct source (e.g., source IP), of the events is important during forensic analysis. Correctly determining the source of events will add information to the overall reconstruction of the loggable event. By determining the source of the event correctly, analysis of the enterprise can be undertaken to determine if events tied to the source occurred in other areas within the enterprise.\n\nA web server behind a load balancer or proxy server, when not configured correctly, will record the load balancer or proxy server as the source of every loggable event. When looking at the information forensically, this information is not helpful in the investigation of events. The web server must record with each event the client source of the event.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000060","uuid":"916BCDA2-6BF8-1014-B6BE-C259C67E97F1","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"An IIS 10.0 website behind a load balancer or proxy server must produce log records containing the source client IP, and destination information.","rule_id":"SV-218740r960900"},{"mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218741","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218741","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000209","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109307","V-100203"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000099-WSR-000061","id":"V-218741"},"classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"916BD5E1-6BF8-1014-B0A9-C3C71387867B","group_title":"SRG-APP-000099-WSR-000061","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must produce log records that contain sufficient information to establish the outcome (success or failure) of IIS 10.0 website events.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218741r1022677","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218741"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218741r1022677_rule","ccis":["CCI-000134"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (W3C is enabled)\nTest                    :   false (Request Header &gt;&gt; Connection)\nResult Analysis         :        '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Connection\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"' \nTest                    :   false (Request Header &gt;&gt; Warning)\nResult Analysis         :        '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Warning\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874101 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : W3C is enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874101 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website logFormat.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'logfile.logFormat'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874101 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal W3C\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874102 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Request Header &gt;&gt; Connection\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874102 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Website All captured of Custom Fields Section\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874102'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874102 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Request Header &gt;&gt; Connection\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'sourceName:\"Connection\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874102'\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n\nResult Analysis         : '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Connection\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874103 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Request Header &gt;&gt; Warning\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874102 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Website All captured of Custom Fields Section\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874102'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874103 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Request Header &gt;&gt; Warning\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'sourceName:\"Warning\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874102'\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n\nResult Analysis         : '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Warning\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"' \n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Web server logging capability is critical for accurate forensic analysis. Without sufficient and accurate information, a correct replay of the events cannot be determined.\n\nAscertaining the success or failure of an event is important during forensic analysis. Correctly determining the outcome will add information to the overall reconstruction of the loggable event. By determining the success or failure of the event correctly, analysis of the enterprise can be undertaken to determine if events tied to the event occurred in other areas within the enterprise.\n\nWithout sufficient information establishing the success or failure of the logged event, investigation into the cause of event is severely hindered. The success or failure also provides a means to measure the impact of an event and help authorized personnel to determine the appropriate response. Log record content that may be necessary to satisfy the requirement of this control includes, but is not limited to, time stamps, source and destination IP addresses, user/process identifiers, event descriptions, application-specific events, success/fail indications, file names involved, access control, or flow control rules invoked.","check_content":"Note: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nSelect the website being reviewed.\n\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nVerify the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" is configured to \"W3C\".\n\nSelect \"Fields\".\n\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", verify the following fields are selected:\n\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Connection\n\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Warning\n\nIf any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nSelect the website being reviewed.\n\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nConfigure the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" to \"W3C\".\n\nSelect \"Fields\".\n\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", select the following fields:\n\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Connection\n\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Warning\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane."},{"group_id":"V-218742","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218742","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-109309","V-100205"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000100-WSR-000064","id":"V-218742"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000210","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","discussion":"Web server logging capability is critical for accurate forensic analysis. Without sufficient and accurate information, a correct replay of the events cannot be determined.\n\nDetermining user accounts, processes running on behalf of the user, and running process identifiers also enable a better understanding of the overall event. User tool identification is also helpful to determine if events are related to overall user access or specific client tools.\n\nLog record content that may be necessary to satisfy the requirement of this control includes: time stamps, source and destination addresses, user/process identifiers, event descriptions, success/fail indications, file names involved, and access control or flow control rules invoked.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (W3C is enabled)\nTest                    :   true (Standard Field - User Agent)\nTest                    :   true (Standard Fields - User Name)\nTest                    :   true (Standard Fields - Referrer)\nTest                    :   false (Custom Field - Request Header &gt;&gt; Authorization)\nResult Analysis         :        '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Authorization\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"' \nTest                    :   false (Custom Field - Response Header &gt;&gt; Content-Type)\nResult Analysis         :        '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Content-Type\"\\s+sourceType:\"ResponseHeader\"' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874201 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : W3C is enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874201 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website logFormat.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'logfile.logFormat'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874201 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal W3C\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logFormat'\n                        : result equals 'W3C'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874202 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Standard Field - User Agent\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874202 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website logExtFileFlags.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874202 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result must include UserAgent.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'UserAgent'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874203 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Standard Fields - User Name\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874202 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website logExtFileFlags.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874203 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result must include UserName.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern '(?i)UserName'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874204 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Standard Fields - Referrer\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874202 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website logExtFileFlags.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874204 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result must include Referer.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern '(?i)Referer'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'logfile.logExtFileFlags'\n                        : result equals 'Date, Time, ClientIP, UserName, ServerIP, Method, UriStem, UriQuery, HttpStatus, Win32Status, TimeTaken, ServerPort, UserAgent, Referer, HttpSubStatus'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874205 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Custom Field - Request Header &gt;&gt; Authorization\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874203 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Website All captured of Custom Fields Section\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874201'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874205 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Request Header &gt;&gt; Authorization\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'sourceName:\"Authorization\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874201'\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n\nResult Analysis         : '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Authorization\"\\s+sourceType:\"RequestHeader\"' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874206 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Custom Field - Response Header &gt;&gt; Content-Type\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874203 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Website All captured of Custom Fields Section\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874201'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874206 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Response Header &gt;&gt; Content-Type\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'sourceName:\"Content-Type\"\\s+sourceType:\"ResponseHeader\"'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21874201'\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n                        : value equals '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      '\n\nResult Analysis         : '[customFields]          maxCustomFieldLength:\"4096\"      ' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'sourceName:\"Content-Type\"\\s+sourceType:\"ResponseHeader\"' \n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001487"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218742"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218742r1022679_rule","rule_id":"SV-218742r1022679","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must produce log records containing sufficient information to establish the identity of any user/subject or process associated with an event.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"916BDD75-6BF8-1014-90C7-C33E8263EC19","group_title":"SRG-APP-000100-WSR-000064","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nSelect the website being reviewed.\n\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nConfigure the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" to \"W3C\".\n\nSelect \"Fields\".\n\nUnder \"Standard Fields\", select \"User Agent\", \"User Name\", and \"Referrer\".\n\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", select the following fields:\n\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Authorization\n\nResponse Header &gt;&gt; Content-Type\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nUnder \"IIS\", double-click the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nVerify the \"Format:\" under \"Log File\" is configured to \"W3C\".\n\nSelect \"Fields\".\n\nUnder \"Standard Fields\", verify \"User Agent\", \"User Name\", and \"Referrer\" are selected.\n\nUnder \"Custom Fields\", verify the following fields have been configured: \n\nRequest Header &gt;&gt; Authorization\n\nResponse Header &gt;&gt; Content-Type\n\nIf any of the above fields are not selected, this is a finding."},{"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must have Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) that invoke OS shell programs disabled.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218743r1156522","uuid":"916BE5AF-6BF8-1014-A77A-F3318D450DEC","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000081","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Remove MIME Type: exe, dll, com, bat, csh)\nResu