Extension:\".wrz\"        mimeType:\"x-world/x-vrml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".wsdl\"        mimeType:\"text/xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".wtv\"        mimeType:\"video/x-ms-wtv\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".wvx\"        mimeType:\"video/x-ms-wvx\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".x\"        mimeType:\"application/directx\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xaf\"        mimeType:\"x-world/x-vrml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xaml\"        mimeType:\"application/xaml+xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xap\"        mimeType:\"application/x-silverlight-app\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xbap\"        mimeType:\"application/x-ms-xbap\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xbm\"        mimeType:\"image/x-xbitmap\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xdr\"        mimeType:\"text/plain\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xht\"        mimeType:\"application/xhtml+xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xhtml\"        mimeType:\"application/xhtml+xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xla\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlam\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel.addin.macroEnabled.12\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlc\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlm\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xls\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlsb\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.binary.macroEnabled.12\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlsm\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.macroEnabled.12\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlsx\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlt\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xltm\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel.template.macroEnabled.12\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xltx\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.template\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xlw\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-excel\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xml\"        mimeType:\"text/xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xof\"        mimeType:\"x-world/x-vrml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xpm\"        mimeType:\"image/x-xpixmap\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xps\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-xpsdocument\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xsd\"        mimeType:\"text/xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xsf\"        mimeType:\"text/xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xsl\"        mimeType:\"text/xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xslt\"        mimeType:\"text/xml\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xsn\"        mimeType:\"application/octet-stream\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xtp\"        mimeType:\"application/octet-stream\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".xwd\"        mimeType:\"image/x-xwindowdump\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".z\"        mimeType:\"application/x-compress\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".zip\"        mimeType:\"application/x-zip-compressed\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".appx\"        mimeType:\"application/vns.ms-appx\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".appxbundle\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-appx.bundle\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".msix\"        mimeType:\"application/msix\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".msixbundle\"        mimeType:\"application/vnd.ms-appx.bundle\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".msu\"        mimeType:\"application/octet-stream\"      [mimeMap]        fileExtension:\".wim\"        mimeType:\"application/x-ms-wim\" '\n\nResult Analysis         : Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Controlling what a user of a hosted application can access is part of the security posture of the web server. Any time a user can access more functionality than is needed for the operation of the hosted application poses a security issue. A user with too much access can view information that is not needed for the user's job role, or could use the function in an unintentional manner.\n\nA MIME tells the web server what type of program various file types and extensions are and what external utilities or programs are needed to execute the file type.\n\nA shell is a program that serves as the basic interface between the user and the operating system, so hosted application users must not have access to these programs. Shell programs may execute shell escapes and can then perform unauthorized activities that could damage the security posture of the web server.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218743"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218743r1156522_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick on the IIS 10.0 site.\n\nUnder IIS, double-click the âMIME Typesâ icon.\n\nFrom the \"Group by:\" drop-down list, select \"Content Type\".\n\nFrom the list of extensions under \"Application\", verify MIME types for OS shell program extensions have been removed, to include at a minimum, the following extensions:\n\n.exe\n.dll\n.com\n.bat\n.csh\n\nIf any OS shell MIME types are configured, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick on the IIS 10.0 site.\n\nUnder IIS, double-click the âMIME Typesâ icon.\n\nFrom the \"Group by:\" drop-down list, select \"Content Type\".\n\nFrom the list of extensions under \"Application\", remove MIME types for OS shell program extensions, to include at a minimum, the following extensions:\n\n.exe\n.dll\n.com\n.bat\n.csh\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218743","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218743","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000214","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109311","V-100207"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218743","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000081"}},{"rule_version":"IIST-SI-000215","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109313","V-100209"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218744","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000082"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218744","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218744","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is not applicable.\n\nFor Handler Mappings, the ISSO must document and approve all allowable scripts the website allows (whitelist) and denies (blacklist). The whitelist and blacklist will be compared to the Handler Mappings in IIS 10.0. Handler Mappings at the site level take precedence over Handler Mappings at the server level.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click \"Handler Mappings\".\n\nIf any script file extensions from the blacklist are enabled, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click \"Handler Mappings\".\n\nRemove any script file extensions listed on the black list that are enabled.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","documentable":"false","rule_title":"Mappings to unused and vulnerable scripts on the IIS 10.0 website must be removed.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218744r1135545","uuid":"916BF2FE-6BF8-1014-9C25-DD6C76F45457","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000082","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218744, SV-218744r1135545, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000082)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"IIS 10.0 will either allow or deny script execution based on file extension. The ability to control script execution is controlled through two features with IIS 10.0, Request Filtering and Handler Mappings.\n\nFor Handler Mappings, the ISSO must document and approve all allowable file extensions the website allows (whitelist) and denies (blacklist). The whitelist and blacklist will be compared to the Handler Mappings in IIS 10. Handler Mappings at the site level take precedence over Handler Mappings at the server level.","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:1701","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218744r1135545_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"]},{"uuid":"916BFB3D-6BF8-1014-BA09-D3FF826070AC","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000083","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must have resource mappings set to disable the serving of certain file types.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218745r960963","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:1901"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218745r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218745, SV-218745r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000083)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"IIS 10.0 will either allow or deny script execution based on file extension. The ability to control script execution is controlled through two features with IIS 10.0, Request Filtering and Handler Mappings.\n\nFor Request Filtering, the ISSO must document and approve all allowable file extensions the website allows (white list) and denies (black list) by the website. The white list and black list will be compared to the Request Filtering in IIS 10.0. Request Filtering at the site level take precedence over Request Filtering at the server level.","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFor Request Filtering, the ISSO must document and approve all allowable scripts the website allows (white list) and denies (black list). The white list and black list will be compared to the Request Filtering in IIS 10.0. Request Filtering at the site level take precedence over Request Filtering at the server level.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server: \n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name to review.\n\nDouble-click Request Filtering-&gt;File Name Extensions Tab.\n\nIf any script file extensions from the black list are not denied, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server: \n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name to review.\n\nDouble-click Request Filtering-&gt;File Name Extensions Tab-&gt;Deny File Name Extension.\n\nAdd any script file extensions listed on the black list that are not listed.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218745","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218745","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000216","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109315","V-100211"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218745","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000083"},"classification":"Unclassified"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nRight-click on the site name under review.\n\nSelect \"Edit Bindings\".\n\nAssign hostname entries and unique IP addresses to port 80 for HTTP and port 443 for HTTPS. Other approved and documented ports may be used.\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nRight-click on the site name under review.\nSelect \"Edit Bindings\".\n\nVerify there are hostname entries and unique IP addresses assigned to port 80 for HTTP and port 443 for HTTPS. Other approved and documented ports may be used.\n\nIf both hostname entries and unique IP addresses are not configured to port 80 for HTTP and port 443 for HTTPS (or other approved and documented port), this is a finding.\n\nNote: If certificate handling is performed at the Proxy/Load Balancer, this is not a finding.\n\nNote: If HTTP/Port 80 is not being used, and is not configured as above, this is not a finding.\n\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.","discussion":"The web server must be configured to listen on a specified IP address and port. Without specifying an IP address and port for the web server to use, the web server will listen on all IP addresses available to the hosting server. If the web server has multiple IP addresses, i.e., a management IP address, the web server will also accept connections on the management IP address.\n\nAccessing the hosted application through an IP address normally used for non-application functions opens the possibility of user access to resources, utilities, files, ports, and protocols that are protected on the desired application IP address.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Verify there exists a hostname entries and unique IP addresses to port 80 for HTTP. )\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/bindings = 'http/*:80:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/bindings = 'http/192.168.40.167:8080:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/bindings = 'http/*:8020:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+' \nTest                    :   false (Verify there exists a hostname entries and unique IP addresses to port 443 for HTTPS. )\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/bindings = 'http/*:80:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/bindings = 'http/192.168.40.167:8080:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/bindings = 'http/*:8020:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874801 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify there exists a hostname entries and unique IP addresses to port 80 for HTTP. \nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874801 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website Bindings\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'bindings'\nExclude Items If        : result matches the pattern ':443'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874801 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result matches regex below\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'bindings'\n                        : result equals 'http/*:80:'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'bindings'\n                        : result equals 'http/192.168.40.167:8080:'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'bindings'\n                        : result equals 'http/*:8020:'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/bindings = 'http/*:80:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/bindings = 'http/192.168.40.167:8080:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/bindings = 'http/*:8020:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'http\\/[\\.0-9]+:80:\\w+' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874802 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify there exists a hostname entries and unique IP addresses to port 443 for HTTPS. \nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874802 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website Bindings\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'bindings'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874802 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : result matches regex below\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : parameter equals 'bindings'\n                        : result equals 'http/*:80:'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'bindings'\n                        : result equals 'http/192.168.40.167:8080:'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'bindings'\n                        : result equals 'http/*:8020:'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/bindings = 'http/*:80:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/bindings = 'http/192.168.40.167:8080:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/bindings = 'http/*:8020:' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'https\\/[\\.0-9]+:443:\\w+' \n","ccis":["CCI-000382"],"rule_id_src":"SV-218748r1043177_rule","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218748","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id":"SV-218748r1043177","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Each IIS 10.0 website must be assigned a default host header.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000142-WSR-000089","uuid":"916C029E-6BF8-1014-BA21-978DFE2CA5FA","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218748","title":"SRG-APP-000142-WSR-000089"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109321","V-100217"],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000219","reference_identifier":"4051","group_id":"V-218748","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218748","mitigation_control":""},{"group_id":"V-218749","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218749","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000172-WSR-000104","id":"V-218749"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109323","V-100219"],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000220","reference_identifier":"4051","discussion":"A DoD private website must use PKI as an authentication mechanism for web users. Information systems residing behind web servers requiring authorization based on individual identity must use the identity provided by certificate-based authentication to support access control decisions. Not using client certificates allows an attacker unauthenticated access to private websites.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000172-WSR-000104, SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000135, SRG-APP-000427-WSR-000186","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (SslRequireCert Setting - Verify Require SSL is checked. Verify Client Certificates Required is selected. Click the site under review. Select Configuration Editor under the Management section. From the Section: drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate âsystem.webServer/security/accessâ. The values for sslFlags must include ssl128. If the Require SSL is not selected, this is a finding. If the Client Certificates Required is not selected, this is a finding. If the sslFlags is not set to ssl128, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21874901 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SslRequireCert Setting - Verify Require SSL is checked. Verify Client Certificates Required is selected. Click the site under review. Select Configuration Editor under the Management section. From the Section: drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate âsystem.webServer/security/accessâ. The values for sslFlags must include ssl128. If the Require SSL is not selected, this is a finding. If the Client Certificates Required is not selected, this is a finding. If the sslFlags is not set to ssl128, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21874901 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'access'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'sslflags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21874901 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must contain text SslRequireCert\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'SslRequireCert'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n","ccis":["CCI-000197","CCI-001188","CCI-002470"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218749","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218749r1111805_rule","rule_id":"SV-218749r1111805","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"A private IIS 10.0 website authentication mechanism must use client certificates to transmit session identifier to assure integrity.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000172-WSR-000104","uuid":"916C0A0F-6BF8-1014-8442-838096023244","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon.\n\nVerify the \"Clients Certificate Required\" check box is selected.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is a public IIS 10.0 web server, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\nNote: If certificate handling is performed at the Proxy/Load Balancer, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting Simple Certificate Enrollment Services (SCEP), this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting Network Device Enrollment Services (NDES), this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server is providing OCSP, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon.\n\nVerify the \"Clients Certificate Required\" check box is selected.\n\nIf the \"Clients Certificate Required\" check box is not selected, this is a finding."},{"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Anonymous IIS 10.0 website access accounts must be restricted.","rule_id":"SV-218750r1138073","group_title":"SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000031","uuid":"916C118C-6BF8-1014-BF93-A8D0798E0902","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-218750, SV-218750r1138073, SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000031)\n","discussion":"Many of the security problems that occur are not the result of a user gaining access to files or data for which the user does not have permissions, but rather users are assigned incorrect permissions to unauthorized data. The files, directories, and data stored on the web server must be evaluated and a determination made concerning authorized access to information and programs on the server. Only authorized users and administrative accounts will be allowed on the host server in order to maintain the web server, applications, and review the server operations.","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:2501","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218750r1138073_rule","ccis":["CCI-001082"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Check the account used for anonymous access to the website.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nDouble-click \"Authentication\" in the IIS section of the websiteâs Home Pane.\n\nIf \"Anonymous access\" is disabled, this is Not a Finding.\n\nIf \"Anonymous access\" is enabled, click \"Anonymous Authentication\".\n\nClick \"Edit\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"Specific user\" radio button is enabled and an ID is specified in the adjacent control box, this is the ID being used for anonymous access. Note the account name.\n\nIf nothing is tied to \"Specific User\", this is Not a Finding.\n\nCheck privileged groups that may allow the anonymous account inappropriate membership:\nOpen \"Computer Management\" on the machine.\n\nExpand \"Local Users and Groups\".\n\nOpen \"Groups\".\n\nReview the members of any of the following privileged groups:\n\nAdministrators\nBackup Operators\nCertificate Services (of any designation)\nDistributed COM Users\nEvent Log Readers\nNetwork Configuration Operators\nPerformance Log Users\nPerformance Monitor Users\nPower Users\nPrint Operators\nRemote Desktop Users\nReplicator\n\nDouble-click each group and review its members.\n\nIf the IUSR account or any account noted above used for anonymous access is a member of any group with privileged access, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Remove the Anonymous access account from all privileged accounts and all privileged groups.","documentable":"false","severity":"high","group_id":"V-218750","group_id_src":"V-218750","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000221","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000031","id":"V-218750"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109325","V-100221"],"comments":null},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000223","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218751","title":"SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000136"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109327","V-100223"],"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-218751","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218751","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If ASP.NET is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nUnder the \"ASP.NET\" section, select \"Session State\".\n\nUnder \"Session State\" Mode Settings, verify the \"In Process\" mode is selected.\n\nIf the \"In Process\" mode is selected, this is not a finding.\n\nAlternative method:\n\nClick the site name.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.web/sessionState\".\n\nVerify the \"mode\" reflects \"InProc\".\n\nIf the \"mode\" is not set to \"InProc\", this is a finding.\n\nIf the system being reviewed is part of a Web Farm, interview the System Administrator to ensure Session State Tracking is enabled via a SQL server, or other means. If Session State Tracking is enabled on the Web Farm, this is not a finding.","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nUnder the ASP.NET section, select \"Session State\".\n\nUnder \"Session State\" Mode Settings, select the \"In Process\" mode.","documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-218751r1043181","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must generate unique session identifiers that cannot be reliably reproduced.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000136","uuid":"916C189C-6BF8-1014-95B5-920650D4CAFF","discussion":"Communication between a client and the web server is done using the HTTP protocol, but HTTP is a stateless protocol. To maintain a connection or session, a web server will generate a session identifier (ID) for each client session when the session is initiated. The session ID allows the web server to track a user session and, in many cases, the user, if the user previously logged into a hosted application.\n\nBy being able to guess session IDs, an attacker can easily perform a man-in-the-middle attack. To truly generate random session identifiers that cannot be reproduced, the web server session ID generator, when used twice with the same input criteria, must generate an unrelated random ID.\n\nThe session ID generator must be a FIPS 140-2-approved generator.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-001188"],"rule_id_src":"SV-218751r1043181_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.site:def:218751"}},{"mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109329","V-100225"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000233-WSR-000146","id":"V-218752"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000224","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218752","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218752","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nClick the \"Advanced Settings\" from the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nChange the Physical Path to the new partition and directory location.","check_content":"Note: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is not applicable.\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\nNote: If this server is hosting the SharePoint Web Services site, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nClick the \"Advanced Settings\" from the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nReview the Physical Path.\n\nIf the Path is on the same partition as the OS, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218752"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218752r1111807_rule","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Verify each web directory is not on boot drive)\nResult Analysis         :        Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875201 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify each web directory is not on boot drive\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : No collected item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875201 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : All Full paths\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875203 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Folder names cannot be in the path of boot drive\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must match the pattern 'C:'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21875204'\n                        : value equals 'C:\\website\\Soteriatest'\n                        : value equals 'C:\\website\\anothertestsite'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21875201'\n                        : value equals 'C:\\inetpub\\wwwroot'\n\nResult Analysis         : Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The content database is accessed by multiple anonymous users when the web server is in production. By locating the content database on the same partition as the web server system file, the risk for unauthorized access to these protected files is increased. Additionally, having the content database path on the same drive as the system folders also increases the potential for a drive space exhaustion attack.","uuid":"916C1F71-6BF8-1014-BB7E-AE20E635C0B6","group_title":"SRG-APP-000233-WSR-000146","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website document directory must be in a separate partition from the IIS 10.0 websites system files.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218752r1111807"},{"uuid":"916C2638-6BF8-1014-9045-8F1E74E70FB1","group_title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","rule_id":"SV-218753r961152","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must be configured to limit the maxURL.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001094"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218753"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218753r961152_rule","discussion":"Request filtering replaces URLScan in IIS, enabling administrators to create a more granular rule set with which to allow or reject inbound web content. By setting limits on web requests, it helps to ensure availability of web services and may also help mitigate the risk of buffer overflow type attacks. The MaxURL Request Filter limits the number of bytes the server will accept in a URL.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The web-site Request Filtering maxUrl value must be 4096 or less)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875301 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The web-site Request Filtering maxUrl value must be 4096 or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875301 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website Request Filtering maxUrl setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'requestfiltering'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'requestLimits.maxUrl'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875301 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal or less than 4096\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be less than or equal to '4096'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxUrl'\n                        : result equals '4096'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxUrl'\n                        : result equals '4096'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxUrl'\n                        : result equals '4096'\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick on the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"maxUrl\" value is not set to \"4096\" or less, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nSet the \"maxURL\" value to \"4096\" or less.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218753","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-218753","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000225","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109331","V-100227"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","id":"V-218753"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000226","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218754","title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109333","V-100229"],"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-218754","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218754","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick on the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"maxAllowedContentLength\" value is not explicitly set to \"2147483647\" or less or a length documented and approved by the ISSO, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nSet the \"maxAllowedContentLength\" value to \"2147483647\" or less.","rule_id":"SV-218754r1156525","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must be configured to limit the size of web requests.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","uuid":"916C2D02-6BF8-1014-837E-F87C075BE81F","discussion":"By setting limits on web requests, it ensures availability of web services and mitigates the risk of buffer overflow type attacks. The maxAllowedContentLength Request Filter limits the number of bytes the server will accept in a request.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The web-site Request Filtering maxAllowedContentLength value must be 2147483647 or less)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875401 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The web-site Request Filtering maxAllowedContentLength value must be 2147483647 or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875401 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website Request Filtering maxAllowedContentLength setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'requestfiltering'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'requestLimits.maxAllowedContentLength'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875401 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal or less than 2147483647\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be less than or equal to '2147483647'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxAllowedContentLength'\n                        : result equals '30000000'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxAllowedContentLength'\n                        : result equals '30000000'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxAllowedContentLength'\n                        : result equals '30000000'\n","ccis":["CCI-001094"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218754","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218754r1156525_rule"},{"discussion":"Setting limits on web requests helps to ensure availability of web services and may also help mitigate the risk of buffer overflow type attacks. The Maximum Query String Request Filter describes the upper limit on allowable query string lengths. Upon exceeding the configured value, IIS will generate a Status Code 404.15.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The web-site Request Filtering maxQueryString value must be 2048 or less)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875501 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The web-site Request Filtering maxQueryString value must be 2048 or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875501 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Website Request Filtering maxQueryString setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'requestfiltering'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'requestLimits.maxQueryString'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875501 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal or less than 2048\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be less than or equal to '2048'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxQueryString'\n                        : result equals '2048'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxQueryString'\n                        : result equals '2048'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'requestLimits.maxQueryString'\n                        : result equals '2048'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001094"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218755","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218755r961152_rule","rule_id":"SV-218755r961152","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 websites Maximum Query String limit must be configured.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"916C33D0-6BF8-1014-8957-A636A9623C4C","group_title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nSet the \"Maximum Query String\" value to \"2048\" or less.","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick âEdit Feature Settingsâ in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"Maximum Query String\" value is not set to \"2048\" or less, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-218755","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218755","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109335","V-100231"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218755","title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000227","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051"},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","id":"V-218756"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109337","V-100233"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000228","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218756","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218756","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nUncheck the \"Allow high-bit characters\" check box.","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"Allow high-bit characters\" check box is checked, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-001094"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218756"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218756r961152_rule","discussion":"Setting limits on web requests ensures availability of web services and mitigates the risk of buffer overflow type attacks. The allow high-bit characters Request Filter enables rejection of requests containing non-ASCII characters.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (The web-site must not allow non-ASCII characters in URLs.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/requestfiltering/allowhighbitcharacters = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/requestfiltering/allowhighbitcharacters = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/requestfiltering/allowhighbitcharacters = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875601 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The web-site must not allow non-ASCII characters in URLs.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875601 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : The web-site must not allow non-ASCII characters in URLs.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'requestfiltering'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'allowhighbitcharacters'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875601 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'allowhighbitcharacters'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'allowhighbitcharacters'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'allowhighbitcharacters'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/requestfiltering/allowhighbitcharacters = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/requestfiltering/allowhighbitcharacters = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/requestfiltering/allowhighbitcharacters = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n","group_title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","uuid":"916C3AA8-6BF8-1014-BCB5-D2EED1793549","rule_id":"SV-218756r961152","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Non-ASCII characters in URLs must be prohibited by any IIS 10.0 website.","potential_impacts":""},{"group_id":"V-218757","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218757","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000229","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-109339","V-100235"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218757","title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149"},"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-218757r961152","rule_title":"Double encoded URL requests must be prohibited by any IIS 10.0 website.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"916C4522-6BF8-1014-A98C-8BDE22368D81","group_title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","discussion":"Request filtering enables administrators to create a more granular rule set with which to allow or reject inbound web content. Setting limits on web requests ensures availability of web services and mitigates the risk of buffer overflow type attacks. When the \"Allow double escaping\" option is disabled, it prevents attacks that rely on double-encoded requests.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The web-site Request Filtering Allow double escaping must not be enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875701 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The web-site Request Filtering Allow double escaping must not be enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875701 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get requestfilter allowDoubleEscaping setting.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'requestfiltering'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'allowDoubleEscaping'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875701 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'allowDoubleEscaping'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'allowDoubleEscaping'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'allowDoubleEscaping'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001094"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218757"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218757r961152_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"Allow double escaping\" check box is checked, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nUncheck the \"Allow double escaping\" check box."},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nUncheck the \"Allow unlisted file extensions\" check box.","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting Network Device Enrollment Services (NDES), this is Not Applicable.\n\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting Azure DevOps (ADO), this is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nDouble-click the \"Request Filtering\" icon.\n\nClick \"Edit Feature Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf the \"Allow unlisted file name extensions\" check box is checked, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Splunk, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218758","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218758r1156527_rule","ccis":["CCI-001094"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (The web-site Request Filtering Allow unlisted file extensions must not be enabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/requestfiltering/fileExtensions.allowUnlisted = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/requestfiltering/fileExtensions.allowUnlisted = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/requestfiltering/fileExtensions.allowUnlisted = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875801 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The web-site Request Filtering Allow unlisted file extensions must not be enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875801 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get requestfilter Allow unlisted file extensions setting.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'requestfiltering'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'fileExtensions.allowUnlisted'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875801 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'fileExtensions.allowUnlisted'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'fileExtensions.allowUnlisted'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'requestfiltering'\n                        : parameter equals 'fileExtensions.allowUnlisted'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/requestfiltering/fileExtensions.allowUnlisted = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/requestfiltering/fileExtensions.allowUnlisted = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/requestfiltering/fileExtensions.allowUnlisted = 'true' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'false' \n","discussion":"Request filtering enables administrators to create a more granular rule set to allow or reject inbound web content. Setting limits on web requests helps to ensure availability of web services and may also help mitigate the risk of buffer overflow type attacks. The allow unlisted property of the \"File Extensions Request\" filter enables rejection of requests containing specific file extensions not defined in the \"File Extensions\" filter. Tripping this filter will cause IIS to generate a Status Code 404.7.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","uuid":"916C4C12-6BF8-1014-8D1F-EFA00AFD188B","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Unlisted file extensions in URL requests must be filtered by any IIS 10.0 website.","rule_id":"SV-218758r1156527","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149","id":"V-218758"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109341","V-100237"],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000230","group_id_src":"V-218758","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218758"},{"uuid":"916C52CA-6BF8-1014-A751-C5E8F81E248D","group_title":"SRG-APP-000251-WSR-000157","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Directory Browsing on the IIS 10.0 website must be disabled.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218759r961158","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218759","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218759r961158_rule","ccis":["CCI-001310"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The web-site Directory Browsing must not be enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21875901 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The web-site Directory Browsing must not be enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21875901 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Directory Browsing enabled status.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'directoryBrowse'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21875901 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'directoryBrowse'\n                        : parameter equals 'enabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'directoryBrowse'\n                        : parameter equals 'enabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'directoryBrowse'\n                        : parameter equals 'enabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Directory browsing allows the contents of a directory to be displayed upon request from a web client. If directory browsing is enabled for a directory in IIS, users could receive a web page listing the contents of the directory. If directory browsing is enabled the risk of inadvertently disclosing sensitive content is increased.","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nClick the Site.\n\nDouble-click the \"Directory Browsing\" icon.\n\nIf \"Directory Browsing\" is not installed, this is Not Applicable.\n\nUnder the \"Actions\" pane, verify \"Directory Browsing\" is \"Disabled\".\n\nIf \"Directory Browsing\" is not \"Disabled\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the Site.\n\nDouble-click the \"Directory Browsing\" icon.\n\nUnder the \"Actions\" pane, click \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218759","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218759","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000231","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109343","V-100239"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218759","title":"SRG-APP-000251-WSR-000157"},"classification":"Unclassified"},{"check_content":"Note: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Error Pages\" icon.\n\nClick each error message and click \"Edit Feature\" setting from the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIf any error message is not set to \"Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests\" or \"Custom error pages\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click the \"Error Pages\" icon.\n\nClick each error message and click \"Edit Feature\" Setting from the \"Actions\" pane; set each error message to \"Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests\" or \"Custom error pages\".","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","uuid":"916C5988-6BF8-1014-806C-C5FF39F0A0AA","rule_id":"SV-218760r1022690","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Warning and error messages displayed to clients must be modified to minimize the identity of the IIS 10.0 website, patches, loaded modules, and directory paths.","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"rule_id_src":"SV-218760r1022690_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218760"},"discussion":"HTTP error pages contain information that could enable an attacker to gain access to an information system. Failure to prevent the sending of HTTP error pages with full information to remote requesters exposes internal configuration information to potential attackers.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (Site error message is not set to Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests)\nTest                    :   false (Site error message is not set to Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876001 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Site error message is not set to Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876001 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Error message error response setting.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'errorMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876001 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result equals DetailedLocalOnly\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876002 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Site error message is not set to Detailed errors for local requests and custom error pages for remote requests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876001 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Get Error message error response setting.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'errorMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876002 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : result must equal CustomErrorPages\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'Custom'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/httpErrors'\n                        : parameter equals 'errorMode'\n                        : result equals 'DetailedLocalOnly'\n\n","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000233","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","id":"V-218760"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109345","V-100241"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218760","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218760","severity":"medium"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click \".NET Compilation\".\n\nScroll down to the \"Behavior\" section and set the value for \"Debug\" to \"False\".","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the \".NET feature\" is not installed, this check is Not Applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nDouble-click \".NET Compilation\".\n\nScroll down to the \"Behavior\" section and verify the value for \"Debug\" is set to \"False\".\n\nIf the \"Debug\" value is not set to \"False\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218761","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218761r961167_rule","discussion":"Setting compilation debug to false ensures detailed error information does not inadvertently display during live application usage, mitigating the risk of application information being displayed to users.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Debug must be turned off on a production website.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876101 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876101 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'compilation'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'debug'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876101 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'compilation'\n                        : parameter equals 'debug'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'compilation'\n                        : parameter equals 'debug'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'compilation'\n                        : parameter equals 'debug'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"916C6027-6BF8-1014-9ABC-8D53C1E93CEB","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000160","rule_id":"SV-218761r961167","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Debugging and trace information used to diagnose the IIS 10.0 website must be disabled.","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109347","V-100243"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000160","id":"V-218761"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000234","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218761","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-218761","severity":"medium"},{"stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218762","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218762","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000012","id":"V-218762"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109349","V-100245"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000235","ccis":["CCI-002361"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218762"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218762r1192782_rule","discussion":"The idle time-out attribute controls the amount of time a worker process will remain idle before it shuts down. A worker process is idle if it is not processing requests and no new requests are received.\n\nThe purpose of this attribute is to conserve system resources; the default value for idle time-out is 20 minutes.\n\nBy default, the World Wide Web (WWW) service establishes an overlapped recycle, in which the worker process to be shut down is kept running until after a new worker process is started.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The Idle Timeout monitor.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876202 (variable_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Idle Timeout monitor.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876201 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Time In Int hhmmss (used to be hh:mm:ss)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21876201'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876202 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : The Idle Timeout monitor shall not equal 0 minutes.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must not be equal to '000000'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21876201'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n                        : value equals '002000'\n","group_title":"SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000012","uuid":"916C6701-6BF8-1014-84D6-AA468A265B44","rule_id":"SV-218762r1192782","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Idle Time-out monitor for each IIS 10.0 website must be enabled.","potential_impacts":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the Application Pools.\n\nHighlight an Application Pool to review and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Process Model\" section and set the value for \"Idle Time-out\" to something other than \"0\". \"20\" or less is recommended if the amount of RAM on the system is limited.","check_content":"Note: If the IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, WSUS, or SharePoint and is not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the Application Pools.\n\nHighlight an Application Pool to review and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Process Model\" section and verify the value for \"Idle Time-out\" is not \"0\".\n\nIf the \"Idle Time-out\" is set to \"0\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218763","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218763r1043182_rule","ccis":["CCI-002361"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Website Configuration setting system.web/sessionState timeout must be equal to or less than 15.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/system.web/sessionState/timeout = '20' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '15' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/system.web/sessionState/timeout = '20' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '15' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/system.web/sessionState/timeout = '20' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '15' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876301 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Website Configuration setting system.web/sessionState timeout must be equal to or less than 15.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876301 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Website Configuration setting system.web/sessionState timeout must be equal to or less than 15.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.web/sessionState'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'timeout'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876301 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal or less than 15\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be less than or equal to '15'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/sessionState'\n                        : parameter equals 'timeout'\n                        : result equals '20'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/sessionState'\n                        : parameter equals 'timeout'\n                        : result equals '20'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/sessionState'\n                        : parameter equals 'timeout'\n                        : result equals '20'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/system.web/sessionState/timeout = '20' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '15' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/system.web/sessionState/timeout = '20' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '15' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/system.web/sessionState/timeout = '20' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '15' \n","discussion":"Leaving sessions open indefinitely is a major security risk. An attacker can easily use an already authenticated session to access the hosted application as the previously authenticated user. By closing sessions after a set period of inactivity, the web server can make certain that those sessions that are not closed through the user logging out of an application are eventually closed.\n\nAcceptable values are 5 minutes for high-value applications, 10 minutes for medium-value applications, and 15 minutes for low-value applications.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000134","uuid":"916C6DEE-6BF8-1014-9D98-D365356EF155","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 websites connectionTimeout setting must be explicitly configured to disconnect an idle session.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218763r1043182","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.web/sessionState\". \n\nSet the \"timeout\" to \"00:15:00 or lessâ.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, click \"Apply\".","documentable":"false","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.web/sessionState\".\n\nVerify the \"timeout\" is set to \"00:15:00 or lessâ.\n\nIf \"timeout\" is not set to \"00:15:00 or lessâ, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218763","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218763","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218763","title":"SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000134"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109351","V-100247"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000236"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218764","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218764","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109353","V-100249"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-218764","title":"SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000237","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:5301"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218764r961281_rule","ccis":["CCI-002322"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218764, SV-218764r961281, SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"During an attack on the web server or any of the hosted applications, the system administrator may need to disconnect or disable access by users to stop the attack.\n\nThe web server must provide a capability to disconnect users to a hosted application without compromising other hosted applications unless deemed necessary to stop the attack. Methods to disconnect or disable connections are to stop the application service for a specified hosted application, stop the web server, or block all connections through web server access list.\n\nThe web server capabilities used to disconnect or disable users from connecting to hosted applications and the web server must be documented to make certain that during an attack, the proper action is taken to conserve connectivity to any other hosted application if possible and to make certain log data is conserved for later forensic analysis.","uuid":"916C754F-6BF8-1014-8793-A39694D30F45","group_title":"SRG-APP-000316-WSR-000170","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must provide the capability to immediately disconnect or disable remote access to the hosted applications.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218764r961281","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Prepare documented procedures for shutting down an IIS 10.0 website in the event of an attack. The procedure should, at a minimum, provide the following steps:\n\nDetermine the respective website for the application at risk of an attack.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nSelect the respective website.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Website\", click \"Stop\".\n\nIf necessary, stop all websites.\n\nIf necessary, stop the IIS 10.0 web server by selecting the web server in the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Server\", click \"Stop\".","check_content":"Interview the System Administrator and Web Manager.\n\nAsk for documentation for the IIS 10.0 web server administration.\n\nVerify there are documented procedures for shutting down an IIS 10.0 website in the event of an attack. The procedure should, at a minimum, provide the following steps:\n\nDetermine the respective website for the application at risk of an attack.\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nSelect the respective website.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Website\", click \"Stop\".\n\nIf necessary, stop all websites.\n\nIf necessary, stop the IIS 10.0 web server by selecting the web server in the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nIn the \"Actions\" pane, under \"Manage Server\", click \"Stop\".\n\nIf there are not documented procedures with, at a minimum, the mentioned steps for stopping a website, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000357-WSR-000150","id":"V-218765"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109355","V-100251"],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000238","reference_identifier":"4051","group_id":"V-218765","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218765","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nUnder \"IIS\" double-click on the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nIf necessary, in the \"Logging\" configuration box, redesignate a log path to a location able to house the logs.\n\nUnder \"Log File Rollover\", deselect the \"Do not create new log files\" setting.\n\nConfigure a schedule to rollover log files on a regular basis.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 web server IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nUnder \"IIS\" double-click on the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nIn the \"Logging\" configuration box, determine the \"Directory:\" to which the \"W3C\" logging is being written.\n\nConfirm with the System Administrator that the designated log path is of sufficient size to maintain the logging.\n\nUnder \"Log File Rollover\", verify \"Do not create new log files\" is not selected.\n\nVerify a schedule is configured to rollover log files on a regular basis.\n\nConsult with the System Administrator to determine if there is a documented process for moving the log files off of the IIS 10.0 web server to another logging device.\n\nIf the designated logging path device is not of sufficient space to maintain all log files and there is not a schedule to rollover files on a regular basis, this is a finding.","discussion":"To make certain the logging mechanism used by the web server has sufficient storage capacity in which to write the logs, the logging mechanism must be able to allocate log record storage capacity.\n\nThe task of allocating log record storage capacity is usually performed during initial installation of the logging mechanism. The system administrator will usually coordinate the allocation of physical drive space with the web server administrator along with the physical location of the partition and disk. Refer to NIST SP 800-92 for specific requirements on log rotation and storage dependent on the impact of the web server.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218765, SV-218765r961392, SRG-APP-000357-WSR-000150)\n","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:5501","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218765r961392_rule","rule_id":"SV-218765r961392","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must use a logging mechanism configured to allocate log record storage capacity large enough to accommodate the logging requirements of the IIS 10.0 website.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000357-WSR-000150","uuid":"916C7C4B-6BF8-1014-808D-ACA61194913C"},{"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109357","V-100253"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175","id":"V-218766"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000239","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218766","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218766","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nIn the \"Action\" Pane, click \"Bindings\".\n\nEdit to change an existing binding and set the correct ports and protocol.","check_content":"Note: If the server is providing OCSP, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nReview the website to determine if HTTP and HTTPs (e.g., 80 and 443) are used in accordance with those ports and services registered and approved for use by the DOD PPSM. Any variation in PPS will be documented, registered, and approved by the PPSM.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nIn the \"Action\" Pane, click \"Bindings\".\n\nReview the ports and protocols. If unknown ports or protocols are used, then this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:5701"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-218766r1111809_rule","ccis":["CCI-001762"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218766, SV-218766r1111809, SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Web servers provide numerous processes, features, and functionalities that use TCP/IP ports. Some of these processes may be deemed unnecessary or too unsecure to run on a production system.\n\nThe web server must provide the capability to disable or deactivate network-related services deemed to be non-essential to the server mission, too unsecure, or prohibited by the PPSM CAL and vulnerability assessments.\n\nFailure to comply with DoD ports, protocols, and services (PPS) requirements can result in compromise of enclave boundary protections and/or functionality of the AIS.\n\nThe ISSM will ensure web servers are configured to use only authorized PPS in accordance with the Network Infrastructure STIG, DoD Instruction 8551.1, PPSM, and the associated PPS Assurance Category Assignments List.","uuid":"916C8343-6BF8-1014-B5CA-89F071A19BFE","group_title":"SRG-APP-000383-WSR-000175","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 websites must use ports, protocols, and services according to Ports, Protocols, and Services Management (PPSM) guidelines.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218766r1111809"},{"group_id":"V-218767","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218767","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000241","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109359","V-100255"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218767","title":"SRG-APP-000427-WSR-000186"},"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-218767r1111811","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must only accept client certificates issued by DOD PKI or DOD-approved PKI Certification Authorities (CAs).","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"916C8D1C-6BF8-1014-A6C5-C97DA94A40AC","group_title":"SRG-APP-000427-WSR-000186","discussion":"The use of a DOD PKI certificate ensures clients the private website they are connecting to is legitimate, and is an essential part of the DOD defense-in-depth strategy.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218767, SV-218767r1111811, SRG-APP-000427-WSR-000186)\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002470"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:5901"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218767r1111811_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server is providing OCSP, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nClick \"Bindings\" in the \"Action\" Pane.\n\nClick the \"HTTPS type\" from the box.\n\nClick \"Edit\".\n\nClick \"View\" and then review and verify the certificate path.\n\nIf the list of CAs in the trust hierarchy does not lead to the DOD PKI Root CA, DOD-approved external certificate authority (ECA), or DOD-approved external partner, this is a finding.\n\nIf HTTPS is not an available type under site bindings, this is a finding.\n\nIf HTTPS is not an available type under site bindings, and the Web Server ONLY communicates directly with a load balancer/proxy server with IP address and Domain Restrictions in place, this is not a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"To add DOD Certificates to the Server, if not already present:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the Server name.\n\nDouble-click \"Server Certificates\".\n\nClick \"Import\" under the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nBrowse to the DOD certificate location, select it, and click \"OK\".\n\nRemove any non-DOD certificates if present.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server to bind the certificates to the site:\n\nClick on the site needing the certificate.\n\nSelect \"Bindings\" under the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nClick on the binding needing a certificate and select \"Edit\", or add a site binding for HTTPS.\n\nAssign the certificate to the website by choosing it under the \"SSL Certificate\" drop-down and clicking \"OK\"."},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000242","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218768","title":"SRG-APP-000429-WSR-000113"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109361","V-100257"],"comments":null,"severity":"high","group_id":"V-218768","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218768","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Notes: \n- If SSL is installed on load balancer/proxy server through which traffic is routed to the IIS 10.0 server, and the IIS 10.0 server receives traffic from the load balancer/proxy server, the SSL requirement must be met on the load balancer/proxy server. In this case, this requirement is not applicable.\n- If this is a public-facing web server, this requirement is not applicable.\n- If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is not applicable.\n- If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is not applicable.\n- If the server being reviewed is hosting Simple Certificate Enrollment Services (SCEP), this is not applicable.\n- If the server being reviewed is hosting Network Device Enrollment Services (NDES), this is not applicable.\n- If the server is providing OCSP, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n- If the server is providing CRL, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon under the \"IIS\" section.\n\nVerify \"Require SSL\" is checked.\n\nVerify \"Client Certificates Required\" is selected.\n\nClick the site under review.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.webServer/security/access\".\n\nThe value for \"sslFlags\" set must include \"ssl128\".\n\nIf the \"Require SSL\" is not selected, this is a finding.\n\nIf the \"Client Certificates Required\" is not selected, this is a finding. Note: \"Client Certificates Required\" can be considered Not Applicable in a Single Sign On (SSO) scenario where client certificates are no longer processed locally.\n\nIf the \"sslFlags\" is not set to \"ssl128\", this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nDouble-click the \"SSL Settings\" icon under the \"IIS\" section.\n\nSelect the \"Require SSL\" setting.\n\nSelect the \"Client Certificates Required\" setting.\n\nClick \"Apply\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nClick the site under review.\n\nSelect \"Configuration Editor\" under the \"Management\" section.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate \"system.webServer/security/access\".\n\nClick on the drop-down list for \"sslFlags\".\n\nSelect the \"Ssl128\" check box.\n\nClick \"Apply\" in the \"Actions\" pane.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 private website must employ cryptographic mechanisms (TLS) and require client certificates.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218768r1156529","group_title":"SRG-APP-000429-WSR-000113","uuid":"916C9620-6BF8-1014-8E32-C8F43DB7D5C9","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (SSL128 is enabled - Verify Require SSL is checked. Verify Client Certificates Required is selected. Click the site under review. Select Configuration Editor under the Management section. From the Section: drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate âsystem.webServer/security/accessâ. The values for sslFlags must include ssl128. If the Require SSL is not selected, this is a finding. If the Client Certificates Required is not selected, this is a finding. If the sslFlags is not set to ssl128, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl128' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl128' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl128' \nTest                    :   false (SslRequireCert Setting - Verify Require SSL is checked. Verify Client Certificates Required is selected. Click the site under review. Select Configuration Editor under the Management section. From the Section: drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate âsystem.webServer/security/accessâ. The values for sslFlags must include ssl128. If the Require SSL is not selected, this is a finding. If the Client Certificates Required is not selected, this is a finding. If the sslFlags is not set to ssl128, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \nTest                    :   false (SSL is enabled - Click the site name. Double-click the 'SSL Settings' icon. Verify 'Require SSL is selected' If the 'Require SSL ' is not selected, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876801 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL128 is enabled - Verify Require SSL is checked. Verify Client Certificates Required is selected. Click the site under review. Select Configuration Editor under the Management section. From the Section: drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate âsystem.webServer/security/accessâ. The values for sslFlags must include ssl128. If the Require SSL is not selected, this is a finding. If the Client Certificates Required is not selected, this is a finding. If the sslFlags is not set to ssl128, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876803 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'access'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'sslflags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876803 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must contain text ssl128\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Ssl128'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl128' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl128' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl128' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876802 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SslRequireCert Setting - Verify Require SSL is checked. Verify Client Certificates Required is selected. Click the site under review. Select Configuration Editor under the Management section. From the Section: drop-down list at the top of the configuration editor, locate âsystem.webServer/security/accessâ. The values for sslFlags must include ssl128. If the Require SSL is not selected, this is a finding. If the Client Certificates Required is not selected, this is a finding. If the sslFlags is not set to ssl128, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876803 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'access'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'sslflags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876802 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must contain text SslRequireCert\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'SslRequireCert'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'SslRequireCert' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876803 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SSL is enabled - Click the site name. Double-click the 'SSL Settings' icon. Verify 'Require SSL is selected' If the 'Require SSL ' is not selected, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876803 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : Debug must be turned off on a production website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'access'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'sslflags'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876801 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must contain text ssl\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Ssl'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'access'\n                        : parameter equals 'sslflags'\n                        : result equals 'None'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/access/sslflags = 'None' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'Ssl' \n","discussion":"TLS encryption is a required security setting for a private web server. Encryption of private information is essential to ensuring data confidentiality. If private information is not encrypted, it can be intercepted and easily read by an unauthorized party. A private web server must use a FIPS 140-2/140-3 approved TLS version, and all non-FIPS-approved SSL versions must be disabled.\n\nNIST SP 800-52 specifies the preferred configurations for government systems.","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218768","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218768r1156529_rule","ccis":["CCI-002476"]},{"stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-218769","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-218769","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"id":"V-218769","title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000152"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109363","V-100259"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000244","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218769","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218769r961632_rule","discussion":"The HTTP protocol is a stateless protocol. To maintain a session, a session identifier is used. The session identifier is a piece of data used to identify a session and a user. If the session identifier is compromised by an attacker, the session can be hijacked. By encrypting the session identifier, the identifier becomes more difficult for an attacker to hijack, decrypt, and use before the session has expired.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Website system.webServer/asp sessions.keepSessionIdSecure setting)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21876901 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Website system.webServer/asp sessions.keepSessionIdSecure setting\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21876901 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : get session.keepSessionIdSecure setting from system.web/httpCookies\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.webServer/asp'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'session.keepSessionIdSecure'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21876901 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/asp'\n                        : parameter equals 'session.keepSessionIdSecure'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/asp'\n                        : parameter equals 'session.keepSessionIdSecure'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'system.webServer/asp'\n                        : parameter equals 'session.keepSessionIdSecure'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n","group_title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000152","uuid":"916C9DAA-6BF8-1014-A37E-A928479E86E2","rule_id":"SV-218769r961632","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"IIS 10.0 website session IDs must be sent to the client using TLS.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nSelect the website being reviewed.\n\nUnder \"Management\" section, double-click the \"Configuration Editor\" icon.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.webServer/asp\".\n\nExpand the \"session\" section.\n\nSelect \"True\" for the \"keepSessionIdSecure\" setting.\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane.","check_content":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nSelect the website being reviewed.\n\nUnder \"Management\" section, double-click the \"Configuration Editor\" icon.\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.webServer/asp\".\n\nExpand the \"session\" section.\n\nVerify the \"keepSessionIdSecure\" is set to \"True\".\n\nIf the \"keepSessionIdSecure\" is not set to \"True\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"group_id":"V-218770","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218770","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000246","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-218770","title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000154"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109365","V-100261"],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-218770r1111816","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Cookies exchanged between the IIS 10.0 website and the client must have cookie properties set to prohibit client-side scripts from reading the cookie data.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000154","uuid":"916CA509-6BF8-1014-90D0-E3E216B0D65E","discussion":"A cookie can be read by client-side scripts easily if cookie properties are not set properly. By allowing cookies to be read by the client-side scripts, information such as session identifiers could be compromised and used by an attacker who intercepts the cookie. Setting cookie properties (i.e., HttpOnly property) to disallow client-side scripts from reading cookies better protects the information inside the cookie.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000154, SRG-APP-000439-SSR-000155, SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000153","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Get the Require SSL setting from system.web/httpCookies for each website.)\nResult Analysis         :        Site/Default Web Site/system.web/httpCookies/requireSSL = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/system.web/httpCookies/requireSSL = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/system.web/httpCookies/requireSSL = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \nTest                    :   true (get the compressionEnabled setting from system.web/sessionState for each website.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877001 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Get the Require SSL setting from system.web/httpCookies for each website.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877001 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : get the Require SSL setting from system.web/httpCookies for each website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.web/httpCookies'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'requireSSL'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877001 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/httpCookies'\n                        : parameter equals 'requireSSL'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/httpCookies'\n                        : parameter equals 'requireSSL'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/httpCookies'\n                        : parameter equals 'requireSSL'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nResult Analysis         : Site/Default Web Site/system.web/httpCookies/requireSSL = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n                        : Site/soteriatest/system.web/httpCookies/requireSSL = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n                        : Site/anothertestsite/system.web/httpCookies/requireSSL = 'false' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'true' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877002 (appcmdlistconfig_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : get the compressionEnabled setting from system.web/sessionState for each website.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877002 (appcmdlistconfig_object)\nObject Comment          : get the compressionEnabled setting from system.web/sessionState for each website.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Site'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'section' must be equal to 'system.web/sessionState'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'compressionEnabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877002 (appcmdlistconfig_state)\nState Comment           : appcmdlistconfig result must equal False.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'Default Web Site'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/sessionState'\n                        : parameter equals 'compressionEnabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/sessionState'\n                        : parameter equals 'compressionEnabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Site'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : section equals 'system.web/sessionState'\n                        : parameter equals 'compressionEnabled'\n                        : result equals 'false'\n","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-218770r1111816_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218770"},"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server being reviewed is a public IIS 10.0 web server, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting SharePoint, this is not applicable.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\nNote: If SSL is installed on load balancer/proxy server through which traffic is routed to the IIS 10.0 server, and the IIS 10.0 server receives traffic from the load balancer/proxy server, the SSL requirement must be met on the load balancer/proxy server.\nNote: If the server is providing OCSP, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nFollow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nUnder the \"Management\" section, double-click the \"Configuration Editor\" icon.\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.web/httpCookies\".\nVerify the \"require SSL\" is set to \"True\".\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.web/sessionState\".\nVerify the \"compressionEnabled\" is set to \"False\".\n\nIf both the \"system.web/httpCookies:require SSL\" is set to \"True\" and the \"system.web/sessionState:compressionEnabled\" is set to \"False\", this is not a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Follow the procedures below for each site hosted on the IIS 10.0 web server:\n\nAccess the IIS 10.0 Manager.\nUnder \"Management\" section, double-click the \"Configuration Editor\" icon.\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.web/httpCookies\".\nSet the \"require SSL\" to \"True\".\n\nFrom the \"Section:\" drop-down list, select \"system.web/sessionState\".\nSet the \"compressionEnabled\" to \"False\".\n\nSelect \"Apply\" from the \"Actions\" pane."},{"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The IIS 10.0 website must have a unique application pool.","rule_id":"SV-218771r1192784","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","uuid":"916CAC4B-6BF8-1014-9169-EE29353E3F21","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The IIS 10.0 website must have a unique application pool.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877101 (variable_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The IIS 10.0 website must have a unique application pool.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877101 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Object Containing the number of unique application pool names\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21877102'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877101 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : This state captures all application pool names assigned to a website (including repeats)\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21877102'\n                        : value equals '3'\n","discussion":"Application pools isolate sites and applications to address reliability, availability, and security issues. Sites and applications may be grouped according to configurations, although each site will be associated with a unique application pool.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218771","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218771r1192784_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the IIS Application Pool is hosting Microsoft SharePoint, this is not applicable.\n\nNote: If the IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange and is not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nIn the list of Application Pools, right-click any Application Pool, and select View Applications.\n\nRemove the filter using the prompt.\n\nCompare the Site and Application Pool columns. If any Application Pools are being used for more than one Site, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the site name under review.\n\nAssign a unique application pool to each website.","documentable":"false","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218771","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218771","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000251","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218771","title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109367","V-100263"]},{"check_content":"Note: If the IIS Application Pool is hosting Microsoft SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.\nNote: If this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nPerform for each Application Pool.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nHighlight an Application Pool and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Action\" Pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Recycling section\" and verify the value for \"Request Limit\" is set to a value other than \"0\".\n\nIf the \"Request Limit\" is set to a value of \"0\", this is a finding.\n\nIf the system must require \"Request Limit\" to be set to \"0\", it is documented and approved by the ISSO, this is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nHighlight an Application Pool and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Action\" Pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Recycling section\" and set the value for \"Request Limit\" to greater than \"0\".\n\nClick \"OK\".","documentable":"false","uuid":"916CB3BA-6BF8-1014-8565-97EC45FA7944","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","rule_id":"SV-218772r1022694","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The maximum number of requests an application pool can process for each IIS 10.0 website must be explicitly set.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218772"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218772r1022694_rule","discussion":"IIS application pools can be periodically recycled to avoid unstable states possibly leading to application crashes, hangs, or memory leaks. By default, application pool recycling is overlapped, which means the worker process to be shut down is kept running until after a new worker process is started. After a new worker process starts, new requests are passed to it. The old worker process shuts down after it finishes processing its existing requests, or after a configured time-out, whichever comes first. This way of recycling ensures uninterrupted service to clients.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (The maximum number of requests an application pool can process for each IIS 10.0 website must be explicitly set)\nResult Analysis         :        Apppool/DefaultAppPool/recycling.periodicRestart.requests = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n                        : Apppool/soteriatest/recycling.periodicRestart.requests = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n                        : Apppool/anothertestsite/recycling.periodicRestart.requests = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877201 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The maximum number of requests an application pool can process for each IIS 10.0 website must be explicitly set\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877201 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get appcmd (Recycling section Request Limits) recycling.periodicRestart.requests setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Apppool'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'recycling.periodicRestart.requests'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877201 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : Web sites must limit the number of simultaneous requests.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'DefaultAppPool'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.periodicRestart.requests'\n                        : result equals '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.periodicRestart.requests'\n                        : result equals '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.periodicRestart.requests'\n                        : result equals '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Apppool/DefaultAppPool/recycling.periodicRestart.requests = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n                        : Apppool/soteriatest/recycling.periodicRestart.requests = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n                        : Apppool/anothertestsite/recycling.periodicRestart.requests = '0' failed test of 'greater than' compared to '0' \n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000252","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":["SV-109369","V-100265"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218772"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218772","group_id":"V-218772","severity":"medium"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218775","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218775","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109375","V-100271"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218775"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000255","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218775","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-218775r1022696_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true ((Regular time interval option) The application pool for each IIS 10.0 website must have a recycle time explicitly set.)\nTest                    :   true ((Specific time option) The application pool for each IIS 10.0 website must have a recycle time explicitly set.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877501 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : (Regular time interval option) The application pool for each IIS 10.0 website must have a recycle time explicitly set.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877501 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get appcmd recycling.logEventOnRecycle setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Apppool'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877501 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : (1 of 2 - Regular time interval option) - Time\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Time'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'DefaultAppPool'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n                        : result equals 'Time, Requests, Schedule, Memory, IsapiUnhealthy, OnDemand, ConfigChange, PrivateMemory'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n                        : result equals 'Time, Requests, Schedule, Memory, IsapiUnhealthy, OnDemand, ConfigChange, PrivateMemory'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n                        : result equals 'Time, Requests, Schedule, Memory, IsapiUnhealthy, OnDemand, ConfigChange, PrivateMemory'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877502 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : (Specific time option) The application pool for each IIS 10.0 website must have a recycle time explicitly set.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877501 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : Get appcmd recycling.logEventOnRecycle setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Apppool'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877502 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : (2 of 2 - Specific time option) - Schedule\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must match the pattern 'Schedule'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'DefaultAppPool'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n                        : result equals 'Time, Requests, Schedule, Memory, IsapiUnhealthy, OnDemand, ConfigChange, PrivateMemory'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n                        : result equals 'Time, Requests, Schedule, Memory, IsapiUnhealthy, OnDemand, ConfigChange, PrivateMemory'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'recycling.logEventOnRecycle'\n                        : result equals 'Time, Requests, Schedule, Memory, IsapiUnhealthy, OnDemand, ConfigChange, PrivateMemory'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Application pools can be periodically recycled to avoid unstable states possibly leading to application crashes, hangs, or memory leaks.","uuid":"916CBB9A-6BF8-1014-99C8-BF5A2925B41B","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","rule_title":"The application pool for each IIS 10.0 website must have a recycle time explicitly set.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218775r1022696","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the \"Application Pools\".\n\nPerform the following for each Application Pool:\n\nHighlight an Application Pool and click \"Recycling\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIn the Recycling Conditions window, select at least one means to recycle the Application Pool (e.g., Regular Time Intervals, Scheduled Time).\n\nClick \"Next\".\n\nIn the Recycling Events to Log window, select at minimum both the events that match the conditions from the previous step (e.g., Regular Time Intervals, Scheduled Time).\n\nClick \"Finish\".","check_content":"Note: If the IIS Application Pool is hosting Microsoft SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If the IIS Application Pool is hosting Microsoft Exchange and not otherwise hosting any content, this is Not Applicable.\nNote: If this server is hosting WSUS, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nExpand \"Application Pools\".\n\nPerform the following for each Application Pool:\n\nHighlight an Application Pool and click \"Recycling\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nIn the Recycling Conditions window, verify at least one condition is checked as desired by the organization (e.g., Regular Time Intervals, Scheduled Time).\n\nIf no conditions are checked, this is a finding.\n\nClick \"Next\".\n\nIn the Recycling Events to Log window, verify at minimum the Recycling Events are selected that correspond to the conditions defined in the previous step (e.g., Regular Time Intervals, Scheduled Time).\n\nIf no events are selected, this is a finding.\n\nClick \"Cancel\".","third_party_tools":""},{"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218777","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-218777","severity":"medium","legacy_ids":["SV-109379","V-100275"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218777"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000258","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218777","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218777r961863_rule","discussion":"Rapid fail protection is a feature that interrogates the health of worker processes associated with websites and web applications. It can be configured to perform a number of actions such as shutting down and restarting worker processes that have reached failure thresholds. By not setting rapid fail protection, the web server could become unstable in the event of a worker process crash potentially leaving the web server unusable.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (An application poolâs rapid fail protection must be enabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877701 (appcmd_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : An application poolâs rapid fail protection must be enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877701 (appcmd_object)\nObject Comment          : An application poolâs rapid fail protection must be enabled.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier_type' must be equal to 'Apppool'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'identifier' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'parameter' must be equal to 'failure.rapidFailProtection'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877701 (appcmd_state)\nState Comment           : Equals True.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'result' must be equal to 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'DefaultAppPool'\n                        : parameter equals 'failure.rapidFailProtection'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'soteriatest'\n                        : parameter equals 'failure.rapidFailProtection'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : identifier_type equals 'Apppool'\n                        : identifier equals 'anothertestsite'\n                        : parameter equals 'failure.rapidFailProtection'\n                        : result equals 'true'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"916CC2E6-6BF8-1014-968E-ED2C21292BD6","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","rule_id":"SV-218777r961863","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The application pools rapid fail protection for each IIS 10.0 website must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nPerform the following for each Application Pool:\n\nHighlight an Application Pool to review and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Rapid Fail Protection\" section and set the value for \"Enabled\" to \"True\".\n\nClick \"OK\".","check_content":"Note: If the IIS Application Pool is hosting Microsoft SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nPerform the following for each Application Pool:\n\nHighlight an Application Pool to review and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Rapid Fail Protection\" section and verify the value for \"Enabled\" is set to \"True\".\n\nIf the \"Rapid Fail Protection:Enabled\" is not set to \"True\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the IIS Application Pool is hosting Microsoft SharePoint, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf this IIS 10.0 installation is supporting Microsoft Exchange, and not otherwise hosting any content, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nPerform the following for each Application Pool:\n\nHighlight an Application Pool to review and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Rapid Fail Protection\" section and verify the value for \"Failure Interval\" is set to \"5\".\n\nIf the \"Failure Interval\" is not set to \"5\" or less, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick \"Application Pools\".\n\nPerform the following for each Application Pool:\n\nHighlight an Application Pool to review and click \"Advanced Settings\" in the \"Actions\" pane.\n\nScroll down to the \"Rapid Fail Protection\" section and set the value for \"Failure Interval\" to \"5\" or less.\n\nClick \"OK\".","documentable":"false","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The application pools rapid fail protection settings for each IIS 10.0 website must be managed.","rule_id":"SV-218778r961863","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","uuid":"916CCA33-6BF8-1014-91A1-F67C09A3BD8D","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (An application poolâs rapid fail protection value for Failure Interval is set to 5. If the Failure Interval is not set to 5 or less, this is a finding)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:21877801 (variable_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : An application poolâs rapid fail protection value for Failure Interval is set to 5. If the Failure Interval is not set to 5 or less, this is a finding\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:21877801 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Full path of each web directory (translated environment paths)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21877801'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:21877801 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : less than or equal to 00:05:00\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '000500'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:var:21877801'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n                        : value equals '000500'\n","discussion":"Windows Process Activation Service (WAS) manages application pool configuration and may flag a worker process as unhealthy and shut it down. The rapid fail protection must be set to a suitable value. A lack of response from the worker process might mean the worker process does not have a thread to respond to the ping request, or that it is hanging for some other reason. The ping interval and ping response time may need adjustment to gain access to timely information about application pool health without triggering false, unhealthy conditions.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218778"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218778r961863_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000259","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218778"},"legacy_ids":["SV-109381","V-100277"],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218778","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218778","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":""},{"uuid":"916CD181-6BF8-1014-AEA4-A029F1CB4E90","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Interactive scripts on the IIS 10.0 web server must be located in unique and designated folders.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218779r1022698","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:7701"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218779r1022698_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218779, SV-218779r1022698, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"CGI and ASP scripts represent one of the most common and exploitable means of compromising a web server. All CGI and ASP program files must be segregated into their own unique folder to simplify the protection of these files. ASP scripts must be placed into a unique folder only containing other ASP scripts. JAVA and other technology-specific scripts must also be placed into their own unique folders. The placement of CGI, ASP, or equivalent scripts to special folders gives the Web Manager or the System Administrator (SA) control over what goes into those folders and to facilitate access control at the folder level.","check_content":"Determine whether scripts are used on the web server for the target website. Common file extensions include, but are not limited to: .cgi, .pl, .vbs, .class, .c, .php, and .asp. \n\nAll interactive programs must be placed in unique designated folders based on CGI or ASP script type. For modular and/or third-party applications, it is permissible to have script files in multiple folders.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nRight-click the IIS 10.0 web site name and select \"Explore\".\n\nSearch for the listed script extensions. Each script type must be in its unique designated folder.\n\nIf scripts are not segregated from web content and in their own unique folders, this is a finding.\n\nIf the website does not utilize CGI, this finding is Not Applicable.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"All interactive programs must be placed in unique designated folders based on CGI or ASP script type.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nRight-click the IIS 10.0 web server name and select \"Explore\".\n\nSearch for the listed script extensions.\n\nMove each script type to its unique designated folder.\n\nSet the permissions to the scripts folders as follows:\n\nAdministrators: FULL\nTrustedInstaller: FULL\nSYSTEM: FULL\nApplicationPoolId:READ\nCustom Service Account: READ\nUsers: READ \nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES: READ","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218779","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218779","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000261","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109383","V-100279"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087","id":"V-218779"},"classification":"Unclassified"},{"reference_identifier":"4051","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000262","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-218780","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109385","V-100281"],"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218780","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218780","check_content":"Determine whether scripts are used on the web server for the subject website. Common file extensions include, but are not limited to: .cgi, .pl, .vb, .class, .c, .php, and .asp.\n\nIf the website does not utilize CGI, this finding is Not Applicable.\n\nAll interactive programs must have restrictive permissions.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nRight-click the IIS 10.0 web site name and select \"Explore\".\n\nSearch for the listed script extensions.\n\nReview the permissions to the CGI scripts and verify only the permissions listed, or more restrictive permissions are assigned.\n\nAdministrators: FULL\nWeb Administrators: FULL\nTrustedInstaller: FULL\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES: Read\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES: Read\nSYSTEM: FULL\nApplicationPoolId: READ\nCustom Service Account: READ\nUsers: READ\n\nIf the permissions are less restrictive than listed above, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Determine whether scripts are used on the web server for the subject website. Common file extensions include, but are not limited to: .cgi, .pl, .vb, .class, .c, .php, and .asp.\n\nIf the website does not utilize CGI, this finding is NA.\n\nAll interactive programs must have restrictive permissions.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nRight-click the IIS 10.0 web server name and select \"Explore\".\n\nSearch for the listed script extensions.\n\nSet the permissions to the CGI scripts as follows:\n\nAdministrators: FULL\nWeb Administrators: FULL\nTrustedInstaller: FULL\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES: Read\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES: Read\nSYSTEM: FULL\nApplicationPoolId: READ\nCustom Service Account: READ\nUsers: READ","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087","uuid":"916CDA9F-6BF8-1014-8590-8950EAFDEA79","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Interactive scripts on the IIS 10.0 web server must have restrictive access controls.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-218780r960963","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:7901"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218780r960963_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218780, SV-218780r960963, SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087)\n","discussion":"CGI is a programming standard for interfacing external applications with information servers, such as HTTP or web servers. CGI, represented by all upper case letters, should not be confused with the .cgi file extension. The .cgi file extension does represent a CGI script, but CGI scripts may be written in a number of programming languages (e.g., PERL, C, PHP, and JavaScript), each having their own unique file extension.\n\nThe use of CGI scripts represent one of the most common and exploitable means of compromising a web server. By definition, CGI scripts are executable by the operating system of the host server. While access control is provided via the web service, the execution of CGI programs is not limited unless the System Administrator (SA) or the Web Manager takes specific measures. CGI programs can access and alter data files, launch other programs, and use the network."},{"reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000263","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":["SV-109387","V-100283"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-218781","title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-218781","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-218781","severity":"medium","check_content":"If the website does not utilize CGI, this finding is Not Applicable.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nRight-click the IIS 10.0 web site name and select \"Explore\".\n\nSearch for the listed script extensions\n\nSearch for the following files: *.bak, *.old, *.temp, *.tmp, *.backup, or âcopy of...â.\n\nIf files with these extensions are found, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove the backup files from the production web server.","uuid":"916CE3A8-6BF8-1014-ACE0-BE56352D2AD9","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000087","rule_id":"SV-218781r1022700","rule_title":"Backup interactive scripts on the IIS 10.0 server must be removed.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-218781r1022700_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:218781"},"discussion":"Copies of backup files will not execute on the server, but they can be read by the anonymous user if special precautions are not taken. Such backup copies contain the same sensitive information as the actual script being executed and, as such, are useful to malicious users. Techniques and systems exist today to search web servers for such files and are able to exploit the information contained in them.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":""},{"check_content":"Note: This requirement is only applicable for private DOD websites.\nNote: If the server being reviewed is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\n\nIf a banner is required, the following banner page must be in place: \n\nâYou are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only. \n\nBy using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions: \n\n-The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations. \n\n- At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS. \n\n- Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose. \n\n- This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interestsânot for your personal benefit or privacy. \n\n- Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.â \n\nOR \n\nIf your system cannot meet the character limits to store this amount of text in the banner, the following is another option for the warning banner: \n\n\"I've read &amp; consent to terms in IS user agreem't.\" \n\nNOTE: While DoDI 8500.01 does not contain a copy of the banner to be used, it does point to the RMF Knowledge Service for a copy of the required text. It is also noted that the banner is to be displayed only once when the individual enters the site and not for each page. \n\nIf the access-controlled website does not display this banner page before entry, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure a DoD private website to display the required DoD banner page when authentication is required for user access.","uuid":"916CEB1C-6BF8-1014-90EB-F469D1A086BD","group_title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The required DoD banner page must be displayed to authenticated users accessing a DoD private website.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-218782r1111818","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.10.site:questionnaire:8301","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-218782r1111818_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-218782, SV-218782r1111818, SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"A consent banner will be in place to inform prospective entrants the website they are about to enter is a DoD website and their activity is subject to monitoring. The document, DoDI 8500.01, establishes the policy on the use of DoD information systems. It requires the use of a standard Notice and Consent Banner and standard text to be included in user agreements. The requirement for the banner is for websites with security and access controls. These are restricted and not publicly accessible. If the website does not require authentication/authorization for use, then the banner does not need to be present. A manual check of the document root directory for a banner page file (such as banner.html) or navigation to the website via a browser can be used to confirm the information provided from interviewing the web staff.","reference_identifier":"4051","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000264","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-109389","V-100285"],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174","id":"V-218782"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-218782","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-218782"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"IIST-SI-000270","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","id":"V-278953"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-278953","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-278953","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Note: If the server is hosting WSUS, this is not applicable.\n\nOpen Registry Editor.\n\nNavigate to \"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\".\n\nVerify \"DisableServerHeaderâ is set to \"1\".\n\nIf REG_DWORD DisableServerHeader is not set to \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nIf the system administrator (SA) can show that Server Version information has been removed via other means, such as using a rewrite outbound rule, this is not a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Navigate to \"HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\".\n\nCreate REG_DWORD \"DisableServerHeaderâ and set it to \"1\".\n\nNote: This can be performed multiple ways; this is an example.","rule_id":"SV-278953r1192787","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"HTTPAPI Server version must be removed from the HTTP Response Header information.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159","uuid":"916CF21A-6BF8-1014-BC48-FE1408001CD2","discussion":"HTTP Response Headers contain information that could enable an attacker to gain access to an information system. Failure to prevent the sending of certain HTTP Response Header information to remote requesters exposes internal configuration information to potential attackers.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Verify DisableServerHeader is set to 2)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\DisableServerHeader'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:27895301 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify DisableServerHeader is set to 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:27895301 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : DisableServerHeader setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableServerHeader'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:ste:27895301 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : registry value type dword equal to 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\HTTP\\Parameters\\DisableServerHeader'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:def:278953","href":"U_MS_IIS_10-0_Site_V2R14_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-278953r1192787_rule"},{"rule_version":"IIST-SI-000275","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"4051","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-283673","title":"SRG-APP-000120-WSR-000070"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-283673","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-283673","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"9168AAFD-6BF8-1014-8FA0-9F1B4506BF06","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This does not apply to service account IDs used by automated services necessary to process, manage, and store log files.\n\nOpen the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nFor each Site:\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nClick \"Browse\" and navigate to the directory where the log files are stored.\n\nRight-click the log file directory to review.\n\nClick \"Properties\".\n\nClick the \"Security\" tab.\n\nVerify log file access is restricted as follows. Otherwise, this is a finding.\n\nSYSTEM - Full Control, This folder, subfolders and files\nAdministrators - Full Control, This folder, subfolders and files (Lower permission levels are permitted)\n\nNote:  A \"Web Administrators\", etc., type group that is an approved group of administrators is also allowed and must be given \"Full Control, This folder, subfolders and files\" permissions. (Lower permission levels are permitted.)","fix_text":"Open the IIS 10.0 Manager.\n\nClick the IIS 10.0 web server name.\n\nFor each Site:\n\nClick the \"Logging\" icon.\n\nClick \"Browse\" and navigate to the directory where the log files are stored.\n\nRight-click the log file directory to review and click \"Properties\".\n\nClick the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSet the log file permissions for the appropriate group(s).\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nSelect \"Apply\" in the \"Actions\" pane.","documentable":"false","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The log information from the IIS 10.0 website must be protected from unauthorized modification or deletion.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-283673r1193224","uuid":"916CF92B-6BF8-1014-8360-F7D406B40A0B","group_title":"SRG-APP-000120-WSR-000070","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:08:02\nResult: informationalRule Result             : Informational\nCriteria                : unknown (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   unknown (Unknown Test Results - An auditor must review results gathered and STIG requirements.)\nTest                    :   true (The log information from the IIS 10.0 website must be protected from unauthorized modification or deletion.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:28367301 (unknown_test)\nResult                  : unknown\nTest Title              : Unknown Test Results - An auditor must review results gathered and STIG requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:tst:28367302 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The log information from the IIS 10.0 website must be protected from unauthorized modification or deletion.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.ms.iis.10.site:obj:28367302 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command against system drive root directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      : for command, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     command must be equal to 'icacls(\"C:\\inetpub\\logs\\LogFiles\")'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to ':'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls(\"C:\\inetpub\\logs\\LogFiles\")'\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\inetpub\\logs\\LogFiles NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(I)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         BUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         BUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         CREATOR OWNER:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls(\"C:\\inetpub\\logs\\LogFiles\")'\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\inetpub\\logs\\LogFiles NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(I)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         BUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         BUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                         CREATOR OWNER:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n             